[SPECIFIC FISCAL RISKS]

This  section  covers  specific  fiscal  risk  that  Kenya  faces  and  elevates  the importance of effective risk management. The specific fiscal risks include:

Fiscal Risks Associated with Public Debt;

Crystallization of Contingent Liabilities;

Fiscal Risks Related to Devolution; and

Other fiscal risks.

[ii. Climate Change Related Fiscal Risks to the Economy]

Climate change occasioned by increased human activities continues to cause global warming that pose significant risks to Kenya's development goals. These risks cause changes in precipitation patterns, rise in sea level, more intense and frequent extreme weather events, and increased prevalence of catastrophic events, such as prolonged droughts and flooding in many Counties as well as vector-borne diseases and pests as witnessed by the invasion of desert locusts in the country and Horn of Africa.

The twin global challenges of COVID-19 and climate change has increased the debt burden and directly affected the fiscal capacities through their impact on tax bases and spending programs and use of fiscal instruments to respond to climate change related effects so as to limit the damage.

In recognition of the serious threats posed by climate change, the Government will  deliver  on  the  climate  agenda  through  a  focus  on  interventions  in  the  FY 2022/23:

Implement  the  Kenya  Financing  Locally  Led  Climate  Action  Program which aims to strengthen local communities' resilience to the impact of climate change, natural hazards and other shocks;

Development of a National Policy Framework on Green Fiscal Incentives to guide and provide modalities for promoting private sector investment in green projects and programmes;

Tapping into green financing by issuing the first Sovereign Green Bond to finance green and climate related projects and programmes;

Development of a Long Term Strategy for climate change;

Development of the 3rd National Climate Change Action Plan (2022-27); and

Review the National Policy on Climate Finance and develop the Climate Finance Strategy.
